  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to a **GMAT Sentence Correction** question! Here is a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcdd GMAT Sentence Correction Question\n\n**Full Sentence:**\n*\"Unable to build nests or care for their young, a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including warblers, vireos, flycatchers, and thrushes.\"*\n\n---\n\n### Answer Choices:\n\n\n- **A.** a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **B.** a female cowbird will use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **C.** female cowbirds use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **D.** female cowbirds lay up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **E.** up to 40 eggs a year are laid by female cowbirds in the nests of other birds, including\n\n\n\u2705 **Correct Answer: D**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd0d Explanation:\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Identify the Modifier Issue:**\nThe first major problem is the modifier *\"Unable to build nests or care for their young.\"* This modifier must be followed by **'female cowbirds'**. Notice that the modifier says *\"care for their young,\"* so it needs the **plural form** of cowbird.\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Eliminate A and B:**\nIn A and B, *\"their\"* (plural) does not agree with *\"a female cowbird\"* (singular). So **A and B are eliminated**.\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Eliminate E:**\nE is out due to incorrect modification.\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Eliminate C:**\nIn C, *\"female cowbirds...lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of warblers\"* \u2014 here, *\"those\"* seems to refer to **eggs**, yielding the meaning that female cowbirds lay the eggs **of** warblers, which is illogical.\n\n**Step 5 \u2013 Choose D:**\nIn **C and D**, at the end of the sentence we see \"including...\" \u2014 this must modify **the birds**, giving examples of birds whose nests cowbirds lay their eggs in. **D** correctly uses the plural *\"female cowbirds\"* (matching *\"their\"*) and avoids the ambiguity of *\"those of\"* found in C.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Corrected Sentence:\n*\"Unable to build nests or care for their young, **female cowbirds** lay up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including warblers, vireos, flycatchers, and thrushes.\"*\n\n---\n\n**Key Grammar Rules Tested:**\n1. **Dangling/Misplaced Modifier** \u2013 The opening modifier must directly and logically modify the subject that follows.\n2. **Pronoun-Antecedent Agreement** \u2013 *\"their\"* (plural) must match a plural noun like *\"female cowbirds.\"*\n3. **Ambiguous Pronoun Reference** \u2013 *\"those of\"* in option C creates confusion about what is being referred to.",
